# Prettier's ignore scope for the whole workspace. Each package's `check` script points here with
# --ignore-path, so build output and generated code are excluded once, at the root, instead of once
# per package. Patterns are gitignore syntax; the ones without a slash match at any depth, so they
# hold whichever directory prettier runs from.

# Dependencies and package-manager state
node_modules/
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Build output — `build` rewrites it, so any formatting applied here is undone by the next run
out/
dist/
.vite/
.tanstack/
.turbo/
coverage/

# Generated code — owned by its generator, which rewrites it wholesale
routeTree.gen.ts

# Derived graph data — written by `code-graph extract` / `apply`, not by hand
scribe-output/
eval/results-*.json

# The published Claude Code plugin tree. ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose: only the one at the repo root
# is the published plugin, and a bare `plugin/` would match at any depth.
/plugin/
/.claude-plugin/

# Prose that prettier does not own. It pads markdown tables to aligned columns and measures those
# columns with a width count that disagrees with itself on the em dashes this prose style uses
# everywhere, so it emits tables whose separator row is a different width from its content rows and
# then reports them as correctly formatted. These files are read in GitHub blobs and Claude context
# windows far more than in an editor, where the chosen line breaks ARE the formatting.
#
# Markdown only — scripts that ship alongside a skill are code and stay checked.
**/.claude/skills/**/*.md
CLAUDE.md
docs/
notes.md
README.md

# Rust/wasm editor extension — cargo fmt owns it
editor/
